# Deliberate bugs, one at a time: each (name, file, old text, new text) must make the suite fail.
# Run from the repository root:
#   python3 apps/api/tests/mutation/mutate.py apps/api/tests/mutation/mutants.py -- uv run --package revops-api pytest apps/api/tests -x -q -p no:cacheprovider
# (the driver checks the suite is green first; do not edit the tree while it runs; each pattern must occur exactly once)
#
# Not listed, because they cannot change behaviour:
#  - hubspot.verify_v3: dropping `signature` or `timestamp` from the first guard (an empty signature never matches the computed one, and an empty timestamp is
#    not an integer, so both are refused a line later; the guard returns early and skips the HMAC);
#  - urls._is_public: the explicit IPv4-mapped conversion (Python 3.12.4 and later, and 3.13, judge `::ffff:10.0.0.1` correctly themselves; the conversion is
#    kept for earlier 3.12 patch releases, which `requires-python` still allows);
#  - urls.ensure_salesforce_instance_url: dropping `if s.strip()` from the suffix list (an empty suffix becomes "." and no host ends with that), and the host's
#    `.lower()` (urlsplit's hostname is already lower-case, so it was removed).
#
# Covers the authentication and security-sensitive modules: tokens and passwords, the role checks, the encryption of stored secrets, the checks on
# URLs the server calls, the HubSpot request signature, the settings that refuse an insecure deployment, and the configuration endpoint.

